WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.021
Week 33: History, Society, and Multiple Perspectives. summarize a historical development distinguish fact from interpretation compare perspectives

2
00:00:10.021 --> 00:00:24.204
Operational objective. By the end of this section you can summarize a historical development, distinguish fact from interpretation, compare perspectives. The focus is useful performance, not isolated terminology.

3
00:00:24.204 --> 00:00:31.921
Language system. Past perfect; reported evidence; concessive clauses; cause, consequence, and counterargument.

4
00:00:31.921 --> 00:00:39.147
Sound and delivery. Paragraph-level intonation for claims, evidence, qualification, and conclusion.

5
00:00:39.147 --> 00:00:48.423
Core principle. Notice meaning first, then form. Retrieve the new language aloud, compare it with the model, and repair one feature at a time.

6
00:00:48.423 --> 00:01:26.329
Model language. La fuente afirma que la reforma amplió derechos. — The source affirms that the reform expanded rights. Otros sostienen que la desigualdad continuó. — Others maintain that inequality continued. Cuando cambió el gobierno, muchas personas ya habían emigrado. — When the government changed, many people had already emigrated. Aunque existe consenso sobre los hechos, su significado se debate. — Although there is consensus about the facts, their meaning is debated. El testimonio aporta una perspectiva personal. — The testimony contributes a personal perspective.

7
00:01:26.329 --> 00:01:36.227
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
